flume 0.19.0's status of a bolt's base place, `flume status --json <place>`, as a host's runner carries it in places.rec
and crew reads its landing fix from it (runner.flume_facts, runner.landing_fix, runner.landing_of; tests/py/test_runner.py,
tests/py/test_landing.py, tests/py/test_landings.py, tests/py/test_board.py; crews-bolt-kind-names-its-landing-fix,
Decision 3).

None of these was recorded, since no host ran crew's kind naming its landing fix when they were made: each is written
from flume 0.19.0's own shapes, `crates/flume-core/src/answer.rs` (PlaceStatus: fix_kind, fix_limit, forecast, fixes,
on_branch), `crates/flume-seams/src/held.rs` (ForecastHeld, FixCause, FixEnded, BaseFix, FixKind),
`crates/flume-seams/src/merge_queue.rs` (Forecast) and what `crates/flume-core/src/fixes.rs` (`decide`) and
`status.rs` (`base_waiting_on`, the fix_limit of a kind that gives one) set, over flume-0.17.0/bolt-failed.json's
base place, trimmed as flume-0.17.0/ is. Each is a base place of crew/bolt@1 named y on bolt/y, its fix kind
flume/fix@1 from flume's own source and its fix_limit 3, each fix named y-<n> at the place fix--y-<n>.

